        "date": "2026-11-19T10:10:28Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui): ribbon cell fill holds its whole label in each theme\n\nThe label of a ribbon cell sits at glyph_px + 2 below the cell top, but\nthe fill and the click target were cell_h tall. The shipped themes set\nglyph_px to 22 with cell_h 30, so a toggled or hovered cell filled only\nthe top half of its label.\n\nThe cell box now extends down to the label bottom and stops 2 px above\nthe caption row. A filled cell writes its label in the on-fill ink, the\nsame rule as its glyph. The cell code moves from painted.rs (468 lines)\nto ribbon_cell.rs.\n\nFixes #2752\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
